## opensift multicontainer apps

# template resource
- os specific feature
- descibes resources for multicontainer app (objects and parameters)
- create app from a template
oc new-app --file mytemplate.yaml -p PARAM1=value1 -p PARAM2=value2

alternative:
- process a template to get a resouce list, then create app
oc process -f mytemplate.yaml -p PARAM1=value1 -p PARAM2=value2 > myresourcelist.json
oc create -f myresourcelist.json

# helm chart
- adopted by kubernetes community
- you can call it a packager, to create standardized, reproducible, and predictable deployments of kubernetes resources

helm create my project
- creates files and dirs:
- - templates - dir containing yaml files for resources like deployment, service, route (special kind that contain references to objects -- golang objects, e.g. {{.Release.Name}})
- - values.yaml -- contains yaml objects that can serve as parameters, similar to ansible variables. Can be referenced in templates like {{ .Values.myparam }}
- - Chart.yaml -- contains chart metadata, version of the chart (pkg/release version) and app version

- verify a template:
helm template .

- helm includes annotations to all resources it creates, so that they can be associated with a release:
helm upgrade <myrelease> . # or a diferent dir that contains the upgrade
helm history <myrelease>
helm rollback <myrelease> 1 # revision number

# kustomize cli
- define multiple resources in yaml, config management tool for kubernetes, no use of templates
overlays - extended functionality
- kustomization.yaml
apply kustomizations:
oc kustomize overlays/stage
- or:
oc apply -k overlay/stage

- add, remove, modify resources
